• Implemented a production-style PostgreSQL schema baseline and disabled runtime schema synchronization.

  Highlights:

  - Integer-cent money fields with DB checks preventing negative balances and invalid ledger transitions.
  - Proper FK ownership, one wallet per user, RESTRICT protection for financial history.
  - Scoped idempotency constraints and replay handling for concurrent deposit/withdraw/transfer requests.
  - Indexed transaction history, refresh-token revocation, transfer lookup, and audit-event queries.
  - Consistent camelCase entities mapped to snake_case columns.
  - Password hashes are no longer selected by default; email is normalized and uniquely protected case-insensitively.
  - Added timestamps, optimistic wallet versioning, token replacement lineage, and structured auth audit records.
  - Added migration commands and replaced the README with CV-friendly architecture documentation.

  Key files:

  - Baseline PostgreSQL migration (src/database/migrations/1736121600000-CreateProductionSchema.ts)
  - TypeORM migration datasource (src/database/data-source.ts)
  - Wallet schema (src/wallet/entities/wallet.entity.ts)
  - Ledger transaction schema (src/transaction/entities/transaction.entity.ts)
  - Transfer schema (src/transfer/entities/transfer.entity.ts)
  - Updated project documentation (README.md)

  Run the fresh-schema migration with:

  npm run migration:run

  Important: this is a baseline migration for a new PostgreSQL database. Do not apply it directly to an existing schema created through synchronize; create a reviewed upgrade migration first.

